{"title":"2014 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The semi-circular region shown has radius 10.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1d38a300c5c7e27f95d646658e5f75798a7844b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); pair center = (0,0); real radius = 1; pair leftmost = (-1, 0); pair rightmost = (1, 0); draw(arc(center, radius, 0, 180)); draw ((leftmost)--(rightmost)); dot ((center)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"172\" />\n</p><p>What is the perimeter of the region?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the perimeter of the semi-circular region would be half the full circle added to the diameter of the semicircle.\n</p><p>The diameter would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb714b3c50cb1e1a18472fb221a0a0b4f19928f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times 2 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The circumference of the full circle would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> multiplied by the diameter, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf5d779e3740a6916b73852f858ab4a72c82e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\pi$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. However, since this is a semicircle, we want half of that, so the second part of the perimeter of the region would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da49d2451807812ad009f97c014db4ab98cfb181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{20\\pi}{2} = 10\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, altogether, the perimeter of the region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a0ad73f2cf6758120494d46b083953970822b4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{10\\pi + 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"83\" height=\"26\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234317\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 30/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1201/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.882      1 2014_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    6.882      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36072:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234317 and revision id 279861. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}